Plain Unicode NFC/lowercase token sequences replace JavaScript matching modes;
current-user-only input, locale filter, priority/matched-key/id ties and immutable
catalogue entries replace sticky/secondary/source policies. Accumulation uses
UTF-16 caps, accepts equality, skips whole oversized entries without charging
them and caps selection at three. Serialization order is separate. No macros,
regex, recursive activation, probability, ignoreBudget, UI or dependencies are
copied. Existing Wisp provider selection additionally budgets the final payload.

Corresponding Source (no charge): every running server exposes /source and a
content-addressed /source/archive/{sha256}.tar.gz download; /docs prominently
links the offer and HTTP responses include a Link to /source. The startup archive
contains this backend's sources, interfaces/contracts, requirements, tests,
install/run scripts and license notices. Its SHA-256 identifies the exact source
snapshot, including reviewed local changes; it is not a floating main reference.
Source trees must be immutable while the server process runs. Restart after code
or catalogue changes. No credentials, dialogue, ledger, .env, cache or venv is
included. Keep this archive and its SHA-256 with every binary/image distribution.
Before network delivery, the operator must download and verify the offered
archive through the same public/VPN access path users have. If deployment omits
required source files, startup fails rather than offering incomplete source.
